WEBVTT

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:04.075 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Guide 2. Open your starter on the laptop.</c>

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:11.895 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>You've practised finding cells in the web page. Now we're going to open the real workbook in Excel. Watch me first</c>

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.655 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>and follow the same steps on your laptop. If I've already given you</c>

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:21.525 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>your own editable copy in Teams, open that copy. You don't need to download another one.</c>

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:28.095 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Otherwise, select Download Excel starter. I'll find a file called Year7 Week9</c>

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.635 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Eco Budget Starter in my Downloads.</c>

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:35.735 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>In this example, I'm using Excel in a browser. I'll open my school OneDrive,</c>

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.165 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>upload the workbook and then open it from there. Make sure you're using your school account.</c>

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:43.450 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Now I can see the workbook. I'm looking for the Eco-Budget sheet</c>

00:00:43.465 --> 00:00:49.375 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>and the headings Item, Quantity and Cost per item. Check that you see those too.</c>

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:55.135 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Keep Excel and the lesson web page open. We'll use both. Now open your workbook.</c>

00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:00.980 position:50% size:94% align:center
<c.caption-en>Don't change any cells yet. Return to the lesson web page when you're ready for the next step.</c>
